VERSION 1.1.0 (2026-07-23)
--------------------------

- Added an interactive Shiny dashboard (`launch_app()`) to visualize the Speech Intelligibility Index (SII), Clinical SPLograms, and prescriptive insertion gains.
- Implemented a fully open-source "Open-NL" dynamic compression proxy prescription, modeling modern WDRC hearing aids.
- Included target insertion gain benchmark data (NAL-NL2, DSL v5.0a, CAMEQ2-HF) extrapolated from Johnson & Dillon (2011) for comparison.
- Added support for demographic variables (`age`, `gender`, `experience`, `config`, `coupling`, `transducer`, `ldl`) to accurately calculate pediatric RECD corrections and age-appropriate compression targets.
- Fixed a bug where overall normal SPL was incorrectly calculated by summing spectrum levels directly (resulting in 39.96 dB SPL) instead of integrating over critical bandwidths (62.35 dB SPL), preventing massive over-amplification in aided SII calculations.
- Fixed a bug causing the insertion gain table in the Shiny app to crash due to missing unaided noise arrays.
- Fixed reactivity issues in the Shiny app so insertion gain charts properly update when adult patient age is changed.
- Improved the Shiny app UI by placing the insertion gain targets inside a collapsible accordion panel.


